CCResPy is a Python code to compute the CCSD linear response function
for molecular and 1D periodic systems.

This program is licensed under the terms of the GNU General Public
License v3.0 or later

In version v1.2.0,  available LR functions:
 DipE : electric dipole-electric dipole polarizability - LG
 DipEV : electric dipole-electric dipole polarizability - MVG
 OR_L : optical rotation beta tensor - molecules only - LG(OI)
   (electric dipole-magnetic dipole) 
 OR_V : optical rotation beta tensor - molecules only - MVG
   (electric dipole-magnetic dipole) 
 FullOR_L : optical rotation full tensor - LG(OI)
   (electric dipole-magnetic dipole + electric dipole-electric quadrupole) 
 FullOR_V : optical rotation full tensor - MVG
   (electric dipole-magnetic dipole + electric dipole-electric quadrupole) 

------------------------------------------------------------------
Python and Numpy Versions:
It has been tested with Python v3.11-12 and NumPy v1.24-26

------------------------------------------------------------------
Input file:

The program reads an input file <input_name>.py, which should contain
the following information:

# Molecule to run procedure on
molecule = "h2o2-321g"
#
# Name of the output file
output_file = "h2o2-321g-forv" 
#
#2-electron integrals baf file
eri = "h2o2-321g" 
#
#Path to scratch directory
scratch = "/Users/marco/scratch" 
#
# Path to gauopen directory
path_gauopen = "/Volumes/gaussian/gdv_j30p/" 
#
# Memory limit (GB) for calculations on Linux platforms
memory = 100 
#
# Energy Convergence Threshold (a.u.)
ThrE = 1e-8
#
# Amplitude Convergence Threshold 
ThrA = 1e-6
#
# Maximum number of iterations
MaxIt = 1000
#
# Perturbation frequencies in nm
WLlist = [1000]
#
# Maximum dimension of DIIS extrapolation subspace
MaxD = 6
#
# Extrapolation frequency for DIIS
RepD = 5 
#
# Perturbation type
PertType = "FullOR_V"
#
# Translation vector (Ang) for PBC calculations 
tv = [4.0,0.0,0.0] 
#
# Frozen core approximation
FreezeCore = True 

Some of these entries are optional and the program will use default
values if they are missing:
ThrE = 1e-8
ThrA = 1e-6
MaxIt = 1000
WLlist = [500]
MaxD = 6
RepD = 5 
PertType = "DipE"

The entry "molecule" refers to the name of the directory where the HF
data is stored: {molecule}_txts, see section "Generating HF data".

The entry "eri" refers to the 2ERI baf from GAUSSIAN: {eri}.baf

The entry "memory" impose a hard memory limit (GB) on Linux
machines. It does not work on Mac machines.

------------------------------------------------------------------
Generating HF data:
CCResPy reads the reference HF wave function info from a GAUSSIAN job,
either molecular or 1D periodic, using the "gauopen" functionality
(visit the Gaussian, Inc., website for information about how to
install gauopen). See the example Gaussian input files for how to
generate the binary array file (baf) that contains the needed
information: <gaussian-input>.gjf.

- To generate the reference data once the baf file is available, run:

  python3 readgau.py <input_name>

  This will generate a <molecule>_txts directory with all the necessary
  files.

- For 1D PBC, the two electron integrals (2ERIs) must be generated
  from a molecular calculation in GAUSSIAN and stored in a different baf
  file: <eri>.baf. The geometry must be built as:
  Cell 0
  Cell +1
  Cell -1
  Cell +2
  Cell -2
  etc.
  The total number of cells must equal NMtPBC as in the PBC job that
  generates the reference baf file. See the example test job
  "h2_eri.gjf" for how to build a geometry corresponding to the
  "h2_pbc.gjf" job file.  The 2ERIs will be read directly from <eri>.baf.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Creating the scratch directory:

Create a scractch directory for the CCResPy scratch files and insert
the path in the input file <input_name>.py

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Running a CCResPy job:

  python3 ccres.py <input_name>

The <output_file>.txt output file will be created with the results of
the calculation. For a molecular case, remember that <molecule> and
<eri> should be the same (same baf file).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Example folder

The examples folder contains example files for the GAUSSIAN jobs to
generate the bafs and the corresponding CCResPy output examples.

GAUSSIAN input job files:
- h2_mol.gjf: GAUSSIAN job file for a molecular calculation.
- h2_pbc.gjf: GAUSSIAN job file for a 1D PBC calculation.
- h2_eri.gjf: GAUSSIAN job file to generate the 2ERIs the PBC_Baf example
- h4-example.gjf: GAUSSIAN job file to generate all baf files for a
  chiral H4 molecule and 1D periodic chain

CResPy output files:
- h2_example_mol_al.txt: output file for a DipE LG molecular calculation
- h2_example_pbc_al.txt: output file for a DipE LG PBC calculation
- h2_example_mol_av.txt: output file for a DipEV molecular calculation
- h2_example_pbc_av.txt: output file for a DipEV PBC calculation
- h4_example_mol_orl.txt: molecular OR_L LG(OI) tensor
- h4_example_mol_orv.txt: molecular OR_L MVG tensor
- h4_example_pbc_orl.txt: PBC FullOR_L LG(OI) tensor
- h4_example_pbc_orv.txt: PBC FullOR_L MVG tensor

